    "raw_graphql_pull_request": {
      "baseRefOid": "d61d8566ec30691645d91727ca7daced073e8f14",
      "baseRepository": {
        "nameWithOwner": "vllm-project/vllm"
      },
      "body": "Fix #38246 — FlashInfer silently JIT-compiles CUDA kernels on first use, potentially taking several minutes with no log output, making it appear as a hang.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `vllm/utils/flashinfer.py`: add `_install_jit_build_logging()` which patches `flashinfer.jit.JitSpec.build` at module import time. Every FlashInfer JIT compilation (attention decode/prefill, MLA, sampling, etc.) goes through this method, so a single patch covers all call-sites.\n- `vllm/v1/attention/backends/flashinfer.py`: remove the previous attention-specific logging from `fast_plan_decode`.\n\n## Expected log output\n\n```\nINFO: FlashInfer is JIT-compiling CUDA kernels (<module_name>). This may take several minutes...\nINFO: FlashInfer JIT compilation complete (<module_name>, took X.X s).\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\nLogging-only change with no logic modifications. Manual verification confirms logs fire only when compilation actually occurs (`JitSpec.build` is not called for pre-built AOT binaries).",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "WJYuuuu"
            },
            "body": "Hi @mgoin @pavanimajety, this is my first contribution to vLLM. Could you kindly add the `ready` label to trigger CI when you get a chance? Thank you!",
            "createdAt": "2026-03-30T09:19:36Z",
            "databaseId": 4153511649,
            "updatedAt": "2026-03-30T09:19:36Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/38462#issuecomment-4153511649"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "WJYuuuu"
            },
            "body": "Hi @mgoin @pavanimajety, this is my first contribution to vLLM. Could you kindly add the ready label to trigger CI when you get a chance? Thank you!!!!",
            "createdAt": "2026-04-01T07:22:20Z",
            "databaseId": 4168078284,
            "updatedAt": "2026-04-01T07:22:20Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/38462#issuecomment-4168078284"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "WJYuuuu"
            },
            "body": "> I am not sure that this is the right place to add this logs. It only cover attn as I understood. Is there more general place what every flashinfer tuning come through?\r\n\r\nGood point, thanks for the feedback!                                       \r\nYou're right that the previous approach only covered the attention decode  path. I've moved the logging to vllm/utils/flashinfer.py by patching  flashinfer.jit.JitSpec.build directly. Since every FlashInfer JIT  compilation—attention (decode, prefill, MLA), sampling, and any future   operations—goes through that single method, this captures them all in one  place.\r\nThe patch is installed once at module import time via  _install_jit_build_logging(), so no individual call-sites need to be touched.",
            "createdAt": "2026-04-04T09:35:21Z",
            "databaseId": 4186842693,
            "updatedAt": "2026-04-04T09:35:21Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/38462#issuecomment-4186842693"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "vadiklyutiy"
            },
            "body": "Could you please share the real output from model run ",
            "createdAt": "2026-04-04T10:14:36Z",
            "databaseId": 4186888005,
            "updatedAt": "2026-04-04T10:14:36Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/38462#issuecomment-4186888005"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "WJYuuuu"
            },
            "body": "> Could you please share the real output from model run\r\n\r\nHi, Here is the real output from running `facebook/opt-125m` with the FlashInfer attention backend on **vLLM **:\r\n\r\n```\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:04 [cuda.py:274] Using AttentionBackendEnum.FLASHINFER backend.\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:06 [kernel_warmup.py:69] Warming up FlashInfer attention.\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:06 [flashinfer.py:45] FlashInfer is JIT-compiling CUDA kernels (batch_prefill_with_kv_cache_dtype_q_f16_dtype_kv_f16_dtype_o_f16_dtype_idx_i32_head_dim_qk_64_head_dim_vo_64_posenc_0_use_swa_False_use_logits_cap_False_f16qk_False). This may take several minutes...\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:18 [flashinfer.py:52] FlashInfer JIT compilation complete (batch_prefill_with_kv_cache_dtype_q_f16_dtype_kv_f16_dtype_o_f16_dtype_idx_i32_head_dim_qk_64_head_dim_vo_64_posenc_0_use_swa_False_use_logits_cap_False_f16qk_False, took 11.5 s).\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:18 [core.py:283] init engine (profile, create kv cache, warmup model) took 12.70 seconds\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe hook lives in `vllm/utils/flashinfer.py` which is the single entry point for all FlashInfer JIT compilations (attention, sampling, MLA, etc.), so the logging covers every kernel that goes through `JitSpec.build`.\r\n\r\nRun script used:\r\n```python\r\nfrom vllm import LLM, SamplingParams\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    llm = LLM(\r\n        model=\"facebook/opt-125m\",\r\n        enforce_eager=True,\r\n        gpu_memory_utilization=0.50,\r\n        attention_backend=\"FLASHINFER\",\r\n    )\r\n    outputs = llm.generate([\"Hello, my name is\"], SamplingParams(max_tokens=20))\r\n    for o in outputs:\r\n        print(\"Output:\", o.outputs[0].text)\r\n```\r\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-04-04T13:34:07Z",
            "databaseId": 4187126120,
            "updatedAt": "2026-04-04T13:34:07Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/38462#issuecomment-4187126120"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "WJYuuuu"
            },
            "body": "Hi  @mgoin @pavanimajety, I've addressed the reviewer's feedback and provided real model run output showing the logs work correctly. Could you please take a look and add the ready label to trigger CI? Thank you!",
            "createdAt": "2026-04-04T14:55:29Z",
            "databaseId": 4187231901,
            "updatedAt": "2026-04-04T14:55:29Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/38462#issuecomment-4187231901"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "vadiklyutiy"
            },
            "body": "Such kind of logging is a bit hacky. But I'd personally accept it, if not following:\r\n - every rank(GPU) print it. In fact for 8xGPUs I see 3 functions from FI and 48 lines of logging (8GPU*2(start-end)). This is a bit noisy\r\n- Even if kernel compiled, FI call `JitSpec.build` and there is logging with close to 0 time\r\n- And most important. We don't catch CuTe DSL compilation. They go different path. \r\n \r\nIt would be much better to introduce this logging directly into FlashInfer, controlled, for example, by env var.",
            "createdAt": "2026-04-08T00:24:48Z",
            "databaseId": 4202997793,
            "updatedAt": "2026-04-08T00:24:48Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/38462#issuecomment-4202997793"
          },
