    "body": "Fix #38246 — FlashInfer silently JIT-compiles CUDA kernels on first use, potentially taking several minutes with no log output, making it appear as a hang.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `vllm/utils/flashinfer.py`: add `_install_jit_build_logging()` which patches `flashinfer.jit.JitSpec.build` at module import time. Every FlashInfer JIT compilation (attention decode/prefill, MLA, sampling, etc.) goes through this method, so a single patch covers all call-sites.\n- `vllm/v1/attention/backends/flashinfer.py`: remove the previous attention-specific logging from `fast_plan_decode`.\n\n## Expected log output\n\n```\nINFO: FlashInfer is JIT-compiling CUDA kernels (<module_name>). This may take several minutes...\nINFO: FlashInfer JIT compilation complete (<module_name>, took X.X s).\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\nLogging-only change with no logic modifications. Manual verification confirms logs fire only when compilation actually occurs (`JitSpec.build` is not called for pre-built AOT binaries).",
    "changed_files": 1,
    "closed_at": "2026-10-29T01:36:28Z",
