    {
      "body": "> I am not sure that this is the right place to add this logs. It only cover attn as I understood. Is there more general place what every flashinfer tuning come through?\r\n\r\nGood point, thanks for the feedback!                                       \r\nYou're right that the previous approach only covered the attention decode  path. I've moved the logging to vllm/utils/flashinfer.py by patching  flashinfer.jit.JitSpec.build directly. Since every FlashInfer JIT  compilation—attention (decode, prefill, MLA), sampling, and any future   operations—goes through that single method, this captures them all in one  place.\r\nThe patch is installed once at module import time via  _install_jit_build_logging(), so no individual call-sites need to be touched.",
      "created_at": "2026-04-04T09:35:21Z",
