      "body": "> Could you please share the real output from model run\r\n\r\nHi, Here is the real output from running `facebook/opt-125m` with the FlashInfer attention backend on **vLLM **:\r\n\r\n```\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:04 [cuda.py:274] Using AttentionBackendEnum.FLASHINFER backend.\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:06 [kernel_warmup.py:69] Warming up FlashInfer attention.\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:06 [flashinfer.py:45] FlashInfer is JIT-compiling CUDA kernels (batch_prefill_with_kv_cache_dtype_q_f16_dtype_kv_f16_dtype_o_f16_dtype_idx_i32_head_dim_qk_64_head_dim_vo_64_posenc_0_use_swa_False_use_logits_cap_False_f16qk_False). This may take several minutes...\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:18 [flashinfer.py:52] FlashInfer JIT compilation complete (batch_prefill_with_kv_cache_dtype_q_f16_dtype_kv_f16_dtype_o_f16_dtype_idx_i32_head_dim_qk_64_head_dim_vo_64_posenc_0_use_swa_False_use_logits_cap_False_f16qk_False, took 11.5 s).\r\nINFO 04-04 21:28:18 [core.py:283] init engine (profile, create kv cache, warmup model) took 12.70 seconds\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe hook lives in `vllm/utils/flashinfer.py` which is the single entry point for all FlashInfer JIT compilations (attention, sampling, MLA, etc.), so the logging covers every kernel that goes through `JitSpec.build`.\r\n\r\nRun script used:\r\n```python\r\nfrom vllm import LLM, SamplingParams\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    llm = LLM(\r\n        model=\"facebook/opt-125m\",\r\n        enforce_eager=True,\r\n        gpu_memory_utilization=0.50,\r\n        attention_backend=\"FLASHINFER\",\r\n    )\r\n    outputs = llm.generate([\"Hello, my name is\"], SamplingParams(max_tokens=20))\r\n    for o in outputs:\r\n        print(\"Output:\", o.outputs[0].text)\r\n```\r\n",
